## 1. General

### GEN-01 — {{ t["GEN-01"] }}
This policy applies to all employees travelling or incurring expenses on company business. Every claim must state its business purpose. Expenses are reimbursed in {{ meta.currency }} at actual cost, up to the limits in this policy.

### GEN-02 — {{ t["GEN-02"] }}
Claims must be submitted within {{ limits.submission_window_days }} days of the expense date. Claims submitted later are not reimbursable.

### GEN-03 — {{ t["GEN-03"] }}
Every expense needs an original receipt or invoice. If a receipt is lost, the employee may submit a self-declaration for items up to ₹{{ "{:,}".format(limits.self_declaration_max_per_item) }} each, and no more than {{ limits.self_declaration_max_per_month }} self-declarations per calendar month.

### GEN-04 — {{ t["GEN-04"] }}
An expense may be claimed only once. A claim with the same vendor, date and amount as a previously submitted claim is a duplicate and is not reimbursable.

### GEN-05 — {{ t["GEN-05"] }}
No single payment made in cash may exceed ₹{{ "{:,}".format(limits.cash_single_payment_max) }}. Cash payments above this amount are not reimbursable. Use a corporate card or digital payment instead.

### GEN-06 — {{ t["GEN-06"] }}
